Fillets: three causes of segmentation faults in TKFillet (mitcad#122).

- ChFi3d_Builder::StartSol (continuing a stripe from its previous surface
  data): when the face found past the contact point is an obstacle but does
  not hold the arc the contact left by (it lies across another edge at a
  vertex), StartSol returned false with c1obstacle set and HC a new, empty
  BRepAdaptor_Curve2d. PerformSetOfSurfOnElSpine then took the obstacle
  branch and walked a surface/restriction blend on that empty curve
  (BRepBlend_SurfRstConstRad::Values). StartSol now leaves HC null and
  c1obstacle false there, so the caller ends or stops the stripe as for any
  other missing neighbour.
- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformOneCorner and IntersectMoreCorner split the corner
  curve at the seam of the face at the end with Extrema_ExtCC; when the curve
  runs parallel to the seam, Extrema_ExtCC reports one distance but no
  points, and Points() read past the end of its sequence. The seam split is
  skipped for parallel curves (as ChFi3d_Builder_CnCrn.cxx already does).
- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformMoreSurfdata read the neighbour face index from
  the first stripe of the builder (myListStripe.First()) instead of the
  stripe at the vertex: with several contours that stripe may have fewer
  surface data, the out-of-range Value() left its sequence with a current
  index past its end, and a later Value() (ChFi3d_StripeEdgeInter) followed
  a null node.
